{"kind":"propose","text":"E3 proposal for the local ClientView. Add synchronous value methods and row fields in @generalbusiness/dap-client/scope:\n\nClientView\u003cD\u003e.explore\u003cK extends Kind\u003cD\u003e\u003e(key: string, act: PartialAct\u003cD, K\u003e): Exploration\u003cD, K\u003e\nClientView\u003cD\u003e.offers(ref: ActRef, keyFor: (kind: Kind\u003cD\u003e) =\u003e string): readonly ActOffer\u003cD, Kind\u003cD\u003e\u003e[]\nClientRow\u003cD, T\u003e.ref: ActRef\nClientRow\u003cD, T\u003e.recorded: RecordedActRow\u003cD, T\u003e | null\nClientOptions\u003cD\u003e.ticks?: (notify: () =\u003e void) =\u003e () =\u003e void\n\nPublish rows and exploration against one immutable cut. Load the checked ES-1 session through the existing reader before publication. Recheck exact replica generation and head, scope/definition, reader and session, plus the pending source versions after an await. Discard superseded completions. If the current view lacks a checked source, publish the rows with an unavailable exploration. A partial act still returns incomplete. The view methods do no I/O, derive a new E1 result at each published cut and never sign. A held result recomputes at each view/context or clock notification. A supplied tick source unsubscribes on close. Without it, the existing clock scheduler wakes at known due and session expiry boundaries. Existing clock implementations keep now/set/clear.\n\nUse the same ES-1 Session and local request-start age as E2, subject to its separate approval. An unknown, mismatched, moved, expired or clock-invalid context gives the appropriate unavailable result. Pass only the value from judgeExploreGrant to the private body judge. Keep credentials, Membership replication and presented grants out. For a recorded row, ref names its actual item and revision. For a pending open it names the exact source key and version. Retain the association to a verified recorded open so a copied pending ref still resolves after recording. A missing or older source version never aliases the row. The existing C4 row lookups, changed fields and draft transitions continue.\n\nSection 5.7 names screen session opt-in. Propose permitting exactly one standing=1 query on the existing endorsed sessions POST in the shared application gateway allowlist and keeping the existing no-query form. The native session endpoint already supports it. Duplicate or other parameters remain refused. Existing room Page and Lending screens are not E3 adopters today. This proposal includes the client and allowlist, with no new route or app rewrite. Please amend if E3 must include a named screen adopter.\n\nFiles are packages/client/src/scope-client.ts, scope.ts, replica.ts, replica-explore.ts, act-context.ts, act-types.ts, session.ts, reads.ts, act-offers.ts, act-rows.ts, act-projection.ts, request-schedule.ts, application-gateway.ts and their owning tests. Reds exercise invariant 12 at a fixed head after a standing or clock change, a changed view, a stale asynchronous response, and close. Compare each held result to fresh E1. For case 7, extend the real C4 Lending witness with a second legal remote edit after the member views the first returned now, then prove a second return before signing and a single later signature when the basis is current. Also prove copied-ref identity and the exact gateway query shape. No changes to ScopeApi, worker routes or derive.\n\nRequest approval of the view signatures, clock and screen boundary, and witness scope. Source follows LV5 and O2.","body":{"to":"planner"}}